      "final_answer": "$281\\text{ cm}^2$",
      "mark_breakdown": [
        {
          "code": "M1",
          "desc": "Calculate the curved arc length: $l = 2\\pi(5) \\times \\frac{230}{360} = \\frac{115\\pi}{18}$"
        },
        {
          "code": "M1",
          "desc": "Sum the areas of the two sector ends, curved surface, and two rectangular faces"
        },
        {
          "code": "A1",
          "desc": "Obtain $\\approx 281\\text{ cm}^2$"
        }
      ],
      "solution": "$l = 2\\pi r \\times \\frac{230}{360} = 2\\pi(5) \\times \\frac{23}{36} = \\frac{115\\pi}{18}$\n$\\text{Surface area} = 2 \\times \\text{area of sector} + \\text{area of curved surface} + 2 \\times \\text{area of rectangle}$\n$= 2 \\times \\frac{230}{360} \\times \\pi(5)^2 + \\frac{115\\pi}{18} \\times 6 + 2 \\times 6 \\times 5$\n$= \\frac{575\\pi}{18} + \\frac{115\\pi}{3} + 60$\n$\\approx 281\\text{ cm}^2$",
      "ai_explanation": {
        "concept_rule": "The total surface area of a prism with a sector cross-section equals two end sector areas plus the lateral faces (curved face + two rectangular flat faces).",
        "step_by_step": [
          "Calculate the arc length of the cross-section sector: $l = \\frac{230}{360} \\times 2\\pi(5) = \\frac{115\\pi}{18}\\text{ cm}$.",
          "Calculate the area of the two end sectors: $2 \\times (\\frac{230}{360} \\times \\pi \\times 5^2) = \\frac{575\\pi}{18}$.",
          "Calculate the area of the curved surface: $l \\times 6 = \\frac{115\\pi}{18} \\times 6 = \\frac{115\\pi}{3}$.",
          "Calculate the area of the two flat rectangular faces: $2 \\times (6 \\times 5) = 60$.",
          "Add all parts together to find total surface area $\\approx 281\\text{ cm}^2$."
        ],
        "common_pitfalls": "Forgetting to include the two flat rectangular faces of dimensions $6\\text{ cm} \\times 5\\text{ cm}$."
      },
