      "final_answer": "$188\\text{ cm}^2$",
      "mark_breakdown": [
        {
          "code": "M1",
          "desc": "Identify formula for combined surface area: curved hemisphere $+$ curved cone surface $\\frac{1}{2}(4\\pi r^2) + \\pi r s$"
        },
        {
          "code": "A1",
          "desc": "Substitute $r=4$ and $s=7$ to obtain $60\\pi\\text{ cm}^2 \\approx 188\\text{ cm}^2$"
        }
      ],
      "solution": "$\\text{Surface area} = \\frac{1}{2}4\\pi r^2 + \\pi r s$\n$= \\frac{1}{2} \\times 4\\pi(4)^2 + \\pi(4)(7)$\n$= 32\\pi + 28\\pi$\n$= 60\\pi\\text{ cm}^2$\n$\\approx 188\\text{ cm}^2$",
      "ai_explanation": {
        "concept_rule": "For a composite solid made of a cone and a hemisphere joined at their circular base, the total exposed surface area is the curved surface area of the hemisphere ($2\\pi r^2$) plus the lateral surface area of the cone ($\\pi r s$).",
        "step_by_step": [
          "Hemisphere curved surface area $= 2\\pi r^2 = 2\\pi(4^2) = 32\\pi$.",
          "Cone curved surface area $= \\pi r s = \\pi(4)(7) = 28\\pi$.",
          "Total surface area $= 32\\pi + 28\\pi = 60\\pi \\approx 188\\text{ cm}^2$."
        ],
        "common_pitfalls": "Accidentally including the flat circular interface $\\pi r^2$, which is inside the solid and not exposed."
      },
